# Build context for the three Python images (docker/Dockerfile*, context = repo
# root). It must stay at the repo root: Docker only reads .dockerignore from
# the root of the build context. The web image has its own context
# (frontend/) and its own frontend/.dockerignore.
#
# A pattern without `**/` matches at the root only, so anything that can
# appear in subdirectories (__pycache__, node_modules) needs `**/`.

# VCS, CI, editors, assistants
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.idea
.vscode
.junie
.claude

# Python environments, caches and tool config
.venv
.venv-*
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.coverage
htmlcov
.pylintrc

# Secrets and local configuration — runtime config comes from the environment
.env
.env.*

# Local data, logs and databases: mounted at runtime, never baked in
data
logs
**/*.log
*.db
*.db-journal
static/data
static/data_old

# The SPA: built into the separate kvuno-web image
frontend
**/node_modules

# Not needed in an image
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile*
Makefile
tests/
docs/
model-generator.py
*.md

# Exceptions: the `*.md` rule above would otherwise strip README.md from the
# build context, but pyproject.toml declares `readme = "README.md"` and Poetry
# validates that file exists during `poetry install`. Negations must come after
# the rule they override.
!README.md
